WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:04.279
(Meghan squeals)

00:00:04.279 --> 00:00:05.407
- Oh, my God.

00:00:08.132 --> 00:00:10.047
I'm gonna cry.

00:00:10.047 --> 00:00:12.020
"What is your idea of a perfect day?"

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:15.030
Today, playing with puppies.

00:00:15.030 --> 00:00:16.758
No one wants to play with me.

00:00:16.758 --> 00:00:18.680
Come here, hi.

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:21.513
(energetic music)

00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:28.860
Hi, I'm Meghan Trainor.

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:31.643
And I get to answer some
questions with rescue puppies.

00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:34.440
Best day ever!

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.360
Oh, my gosh, you're all so cute, okay.

00:00:37.360 --> 00:00:39.130
Aw, they're fighting, aw.

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:40.720
That's so cute, okay.

00:00:40.720 --> 00:00:42.667
I'm gonna answer these
questions, here we go.

00:00:42.667 --> 00:00:45.277
"What's the biggest
thing you've splurged on

00:00:45.277 --> 00:00:47.390
"since you became famous?"

00:00:47.390 --> 00:00:50.440
I bought a Tesla!

00:00:50.440 --> 00:00:52.920
I did it, oh, no, now
they're gonna eat the papers.

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:55.403
I just did that for myself, yes, I did.

00:00:56.640 --> 00:01:00.047
They have plans, look at them, hi.

00:01:00.047 --> 00:01:01.487
"Did you grow up watching your fiance

00:01:01.487 --> 00:01:03.320
"in the Spy Kids like the rest of us did?"

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:05.820
- Whoa.
- Of course I did.

00:01:05.820 --> 00:01:07.010
The first time I ever met him

00:01:07.010 --> 00:01:09.420
was at a party two years
before our first date.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:11.180
A song writing party I was at.

00:01:11.180 --> 00:01:14.160
And I went up to him,
I went right up to him,

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:16.700
and I've never done that
to like a celebrity before,

00:01:16.700 --> 00:01:19.330
and was like, "Excuse
me, are you Spy Kids?"

00:01:19.330 --> 00:01:21.180
And he was like, "Yeah."

00:01:21.180 --> 00:01:24.520
And I would yell, check
this out guy, "Spy Kids!"

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:26.320
And he would yell, "Meghan!"

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:28.600
And I was like, "He remembered my name."

00:01:28.600 --> 00:01:30.330
So, I had my whole fan girl moment.

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:32.190
And sometimes I told
him when we were dating,

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:35.110
in the early days, that
sometimes when he laughed,

00:01:35.110 --> 00:01:39.190
I would see Juni, little
young Juni (chuckles) Cortez.

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:40.550
And I had to get over that.

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:44.060
Now I see a man, a very handsome man

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:45.680
that I love very much.

00:01:45.680 --> 00:01:47.377
Okay, "Which music video of yours

00:01:47.377 --> 00:01:49.487
"is your all-time favorite?

00:01:49.487 --> 00:01:52.590
"Are there any that you would
change now if you could?"

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:54.010
Oh, great question.

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:57.430
I would say my favorite
is "No Excuses" right now

00:01:57.430 --> 00:01:59.030
'cause we worked really hard on that one,

00:01:59.030 --> 00:02:02.360
and there's a lot of me's
and I got to be triplets.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:04.990
Hi, and which one I would change.

00:02:04.990 --> 00:02:06.840
I don't know, I probably
wouldn't change any.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:09.290
Oh, "Bass", yeah, even
though that was a big video,

00:02:09.290 --> 00:02:12.480
I feel like I didn't have
makeup squad at that time,

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:14.520
and I was very new to everything,

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:17.020
and I didn't say a lot of what I wanted,

00:02:17.020 --> 00:02:20.190
and I would've changed,
I think, some looks up.

00:02:20.190 --> 00:02:23.840
But they're so famous and
iconic that it worked out well.

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:25.837
Okay, "What is the most ridiculous

00:02:25.837 --> 00:02:27.010
"rumor you've heard about yourself?"

00:02:27.010 --> 00:02:29.210
That I died, got a lot of those.

00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:32.160
Got a lot of I'm pregnant and I'm dead.

00:02:32.160 --> 00:02:34.820
So, I'm good, I'm healthy, I'm alive.

00:02:34.820 --> 00:02:39.600
I sent the passing of our
sweet, beloved Meghan Trainor,

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:41.247
sent that article to my
mom, and she was like,

00:02:41.247 --> 00:02:44.430
"This is not even funny,
do not send me this."

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:48.440
So, don't say that if I'm alive.

00:02:48.440 --> 00:02:53.390
Oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, oh, yeah.

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:56.240
Oh, that some sweet lovin', oh.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:00.277
Hi, okay, okay, where's
my question, where is it?

00:03:00.277 --> 00:03:03.517
"What was your inspiration behind

00:03:03.517 --> 00:03:05.060
"your new single, 'No Excuses'?"

00:03:05.060 --> 00:03:07.970
I wanted to write a big
anthem for my way back,

00:03:07.970 --> 00:03:09.570
and I wanted it to mean something,

00:03:09.570 --> 00:03:12.390
and I've had personal
experiences with respect

00:03:12.390 --> 00:03:14.990
and people respecting
each other of all ages.

00:03:14.990 --> 00:03:16.850
So, I wanted to write a fun, happy song

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:18.930
that was like a modern day version

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:21.970
of R-E-S-P-E-C-T, respect me, you know?

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:23.190
There's no excuse.

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:26.040
Treat others the way you want
to be treated like puppies.

00:03:26.930 --> 00:03:31.620
You are so pretty, you are
so pretty, what is this face?

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:34.457
You're a special mix, look at you, okay.

00:03:34.457 --> 00:03:36.950
"What is your favorite memory
while writing this album?"

00:03:36.950 --> 00:03:39.721
My favorite memory (gasps)
while writing this album

00:03:39.721 --> 00:03:44.100
(chuckles) is having my
family singing on backgrounds,

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:47.173
and trying to record
them, and not make a mess.

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:49.813
Oh, you want this?

00:03:49.813 --> 00:03:51.850
It's really hard to focus on the questions

00:03:51.850 --> 00:03:53.530
when you got puppies in your face.

00:03:53.530 --> 00:03:55.083
Oh, yeah, you want a question?

00:03:55.960 --> 00:03:57.470
Okay, sweet thing.

00:03:57.470 --> 00:03:58.963
Oh, you get one too, okay.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:00.893
Okay, here's one.

00:04:02.077 --> 00:04:04.907
"Can you give us a hint as to what

00:04:04.907 --> 00:04:06.787
"the rest of the album will be like?

00:04:06.787 --> 00:04:08.730
"And inspiration behind
some of the songs?"

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:13.620
Okay, the rest of the album's
gonna be pop, pop anthems.

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:16.890
A lot about love, a lot about happiness.

00:04:16.890 --> 00:04:19.430
The song is about loving yourself.

00:04:19.430 --> 00:04:21.380
Every song is like a
dance song, except one.

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:23.180
There's a beautiful ballad in there.

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:25.210
And the inspiration was my life,

00:04:25.210 --> 00:04:27.651
and experiences I go through.

00:04:27.651 --> 00:04:29.033
(growls) What are you doing?

00:04:29.033 --> 00:04:30.520
(growls) Come here.

00:04:30.520 --> 00:04:32.840
Hi, hi, hi, no biting, sir.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:34.807
Okay, "Who has been the most inspiring

00:04:34.807 --> 00:04:36.920
"to you during your
creation of your new album?"

00:04:36.920 --> 00:04:38.530
I listened to a lot of ABBA before this.

00:04:38.530 --> 00:04:43.449
And OG pop, like young
Britney Spears, like--

00:04:43.449 --> 00:04:44.730
♪ She's so lucky, bum, bum, bum ♪

00:04:44.730 --> 00:04:46.193
Listened to that a lot.

00:04:46.193 --> 00:04:47.850
I love how the backgrounds are in there.

00:04:47.850 --> 00:04:50.173
I love the vocalists all over these songs.

00:04:51.550 --> 00:04:54.170
Max Martin back in the
day, that was my jam,

00:04:54.170 --> 00:04:57.040
that's what I grew up on,
NSYNC and Backstreet Boys.

00:04:57.040 --> 00:04:58.770
I listened to a lot of
that when I was writing.

00:04:58.770 --> 00:05:01.750
So, you'll hear big pop songs like that.

00:05:01.750 --> 00:05:04.440
Yes, you will, yes, you will.

00:05:04.440 --> 00:05:05.780
Come on in, okay.

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:07.680
Is it 'cause you want this?

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:09.913
That's why you want me, okay, here we go.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:13.887
All right, "If you could change one thing

00:05:13.887 --> 00:05:16.283
"you've done in the
past, what would it be?"

00:05:16.283 --> 00:05:17.510
(upbeat music)

00:05:17.510 --> 00:05:19.130
Yeah, many.

00:05:19.130 --> 00:05:21.130
If I could change one thing in the past?

00:05:22.385 --> 00:05:24.770
I wouldn't 'cause I'm here now

00:05:24.770 --> 00:05:25.620
and that's all that matters (gasps).

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:28.090
Did you want this question?

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:31.017
You can't eat it, let me read it first.

00:05:31.017 --> 00:05:32.587
"What's your favorite
song to preform live?'

00:05:32.587 --> 00:05:34.410
"No Excuses" 'cause it's easier

00:05:34.410 --> 00:05:36.950
than every other song I've written.

00:05:36.950 --> 00:05:38.400
And it's actually a fun time.

00:05:40.060 --> 00:05:42.740
Girls, guys, come here.

00:05:42.740 --> 00:05:46.430
I got the bag, oh, look,
it's my hand, okay.

00:05:46.430 --> 00:05:47.607
Okay, "Which celebrity left you

00:05:47.607 --> 00:05:49.130
"starstruck when you met them?"

00:05:49.130 --> 00:05:50.200
Adele, yep.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:51.970
Oh, you got in the bag,
don't get in the bag.

00:05:51.970 --> 00:05:53.910
Here you go, here you go.

00:05:53.910 --> 00:05:56.120
Everyone calm down, okay?

00:05:56.120 --> 00:05:59.700
This one's chill, chill out, yeah.

00:05:59.700 --> 00:06:03.087
Okay, "Your fiance, Daryl
Sabara sings on your new album.

00:06:03.087 --> 00:06:05.910
"What was it like to work
together professionally?"

00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:07.580
Aw, it was always fun,

00:06:07.580 --> 00:06:09.540
it didn't fee like professional work.

00:06:09.540 --> 00:06:12.563
He was really good, he's a good singer.

00:06:13.530 --> 00:06:17.920
Something's happening here
that is rated R right now.

00:06:17.920 --> 00:06:21.297
Are you a little freak, you
little freak (chuckles)?

00:06:22.750 --> 00:06:25.727
Oh, oh, yes, babies, yes, come on in.

00:06:25.727 --> 00:06:29.880
"Which celeb would you die to
have sing at your wedding?"

00:06:29.880 --> 00:06:33.750
Oh, Lord, can they be dead or alive?

00:06:33.750 --> 00:06:35.640
I would die to have Frank Sinatra,

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:37.050
even though can't do that one.

00:06:37.050 --> 00:06:40.350
Who should sing at our
wedding that won't (laughs)?

00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:43.510
Oh, Bruno, Bruno, come sing for me.

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:44.640
Sing at my wedding!

00:06:44.640 --> 00:06:46.680
I went to your concert, you know?

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:49.527
It's like the same, okay.

00:06:49.527 --> 00:06:53.720
"What is your favorite
lyric of all of your songs?"

00:06:53.720 --> 00:06:56.017
Is, "We're not promised tomorrow,"

00:06:56.017 --> 00:06:57.310
"Like, I'm Gonna Lose You."

00:06:57.310 --> 00:06:58.963
That song, them lyrics.

00:07:00.637 --> 00:07:01.857
"If you could go back and give

00:07:01.857 --> 00:07:05.560
"your teen self some
advice, what would you say?"

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:08.977
I would say, "Don't stress so much.

00:07:08.977 --> 00:07:10.827
"Stop having so much stress.

00:07:10.827 --> 00:07:13.087
"Like, relax, you're a kid.

00:07:13.087 --> 00:07:16.430
"You're not an adult yet,
adult life is much different."

00:07:16.430 --> 00:07:19.280
But also, "Time will heal all."

00:07:19.280 --> 00:07:21.547
And, "You look better when you get older,

00:07:21.547 --> 00:07:24.530
"so don't freak out, you know?"

00:07:24.530 --> 00:07:27.050
I think we did it, kids.

00:07:27.050 --> 00:07:29.860
If you wanna adopt these
amazing, sweet puppies,

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:33.950
go to North Shore Animal League America.

00:07:33.950 --> 00:07:35.250
That's all you have to do,

00:07:35.250 --> 00:07:36.913
and you can take one of these home.

00:07:38.079 --> 00:07:40.835
(squeals) You're excited, you want a home?

00:07:40.835 --> 00:07:43.918
(lighthearted music)

